Z||000002||stimpy||03-15-2001||09:37 AM||||hehe, Yeah, the foam is best done one side at a time. But it looks like it's coming along well. Is it done yet?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||03-15-2001||10:50 AM||||The box is covered in 3 layers of 'glass, 4 in some place.  I just need to find some MDF for the face, get a speaker grill and a terminal cup and it'll be done.  Just haven't gotten around to it..||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-15-2001||01:39 PM||||18mm Birch plywood is better for the face.. it'll take more moisture/abuse than MDF and being at your feet it'll get wet!  and NO, it doesn't rattle like cheap plywood. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||03-15-2001||06:31 PM||||lookin' good.<BR>the box i mean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>i didn't use foam spray in mine. how does it help? i've just about got mine done so i don't think it will help me now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||14
Z||000006||Standard||03-15-2001||10:38 PM||||The only reason you need it is the stiffen up the construction paper so you can lay the fiberglass on it and not lose the shape... If I didn't have to use it I wouldn't have... but with everything I've learned from doing this one the next one will be much easier.||||reg||1
